cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "goalbench: a reproducible benchmark of choice-style deciders for customer-goal classification in Brazilian Portuguese"
type: software
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-10-08
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/fuljorge/goal-classification-bench"
authors:
  - family-names: "Jorge da Silva"
    given-names: "Fulvio"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0475-9343"
abstract: >-
  goalbench measures small "decider" models that answer typed choice questions (Laya,
  Strands Decider) on customer-goal classification in Brazilian Portuguese, inside a
  two-stage pipeline: an embedding shortlist of 10 goals followed by the decider, with a
  calibrated combination fitted by cross-validation. Runs log every phrase, control for
  option-order (position) bias, and report Wilson intervals and exact McNemar tests. A
  parallel English translation of the dataset measures the accuracy lost in Brazilian
  Portuguese and the gain from a language-specific checkpoint.
keywords:
  - intent classification
  - goal classification
  - Brazilian Portuguese
  - multilingual evaluation
  - benchmark
  - Laya
  - Strands Decider
  - embeddings
  - calibration
